-can make the normalized old conflict small when \(L\gg N\), but then a path-aware horizon-oblivious policy can quote near \(c_0\) in the first zero block and near \(c_1\) in the long later block; the old loss is diluted by the many new quote opportunities. The equality \(D_{N+L+2}=N\,c_0(c_1-c_0)/c_1\) is plausible in the formal model but still needs an all-intermediate-horizon proof before being promoted as exact. The broader lesson is sound: close conflicts make \(D_n\) linear, while conflicts far enough apart to hide from \(D_n/n\) may also become easy for a fixed path-aware policy.
